# All ten images build with `context: .` (docker-compose.yml), so without this
# file Docker ships the entire working tree to the daemon ten times per build —
# about 38 MB each, 31 MB of which is the host .venv the images never touch.
#
# Everything excluded here is verified unreferenced by any Dockerfile. config/,
# data/ and tunnel/ reach the containers as runtime bind mounts, not COPY, and
# scripts/ and tests/ run on the host. What the images actually consume is
# libs/, services/<name>/ and apps/<name>/, which are all still in context.

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.venv

# Runtime bind mounts — see docker-compose.yml. data/ also holds the signing key
# and the audit log, which have no business in a build context.
config/
data/
tunnel/

# Host-only.
scripts/
tests/

# Documentation and tooling. Note this does NOT exclude *.md generally:
# apps/*/chainlit.md is the welcome screen and is copied into both UI images.
docs/
reports/
.claude/

# Never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*

**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.files/
**/.chainlit/translations/
*.pyc
